  "as_of_notes": "Registered-voter counts are 'as of 12/05/2024 10:16 AM' per the report footer, reflecting the Missouri Centralized Voter Registration list at certification of the November 5, 2024 General Election. The report's 'Registered Voters' column = Active + Inactive voters. Statewide total 4,433,383 is the sum of all listed jurisdictions and matches the report's printed total exactly.",
  "data_quality": "high",
  "notes": "Source is the latest official statewide registration breakdown published by the Missouri SOS (the dedicated 'Registered Voters in Missouri' archive at sos.mo.gov/elections/registeredvoters only extends through 2022; the Nov 2024 Official Voter Turnout Report is the most recent official by-jurisdiction registration data). Missouri does NOT register voters by party, so by_party fields are null. The report lists 116 election jurisdictions: 114 counties + the City of St. Louis (an independent city, FIPS 29510) + Kansas City. Kansas City is reported as a SEPARATE election authority (it has its own Board of Election Commissioners) whose registrants reside within Jackson, Clay, Platte and Cass counties; it has no county FIPS so fips is null for that unit. All 116 units are retained so the sum reconciles to the official statewide total of 4,433,383; dropping Kansas City (229,293 registered) would understate the total. The 115 standard county-level units requested (114 counties + St. Louis City) are all present and individually FIPS-coded. St. Louis City (29510) is distinct from St. Louis County (29189: 745,425 registered)."
